        "title": "Scheduled Freebucks repricing for three models added to common",
        "summary": "A new leaf module, common/src/constants/freebuff-price-schedule.ts, introduces a single dated repricing scheduled for 2026-10-23T00:00:00Z, where new sessions on three rows change cost while already-admitted sessions keep their original price. The frozen FREEBUFF_SCHEDULED_PRICES map sets google/gemini-4-argon at 250, openai/gpt-6.1-sol at 200, and fbc/claude-haiku-5.5 at 100 Freebucks. The helper scheduledFreebucksPrice returns the new multiplier only when the current time is at or past FREEBUFF_REPRICE_AT, and freebuffRepriceAnnounced controls whether the pre-repricing announcement pills remain visible. Compiled model rows read the price through freebucksSessionPrice, while the catalog-only Claude Haiku 5.5 full row reads it through its catalog entry on every refresh.",
